('ILL26-000313','A-level','Physics','Quantum physics','constructed_response','State the photoelectric effect and explain the threshold frequency.','Electrons are emitted from a metal surface when light above a certain frequency shines on it. The threshold frequency is the minimum frequency for emission: a photon''s energy hf must be at least the work function φ, so f₀ = φ/h. Below f₀ no electrons are emitted, however intense the light.','Subject-specialist worked solution or mark scheme required before publication.',2,'intermediate','Illumed original generated draft','original content; verify before release','ai_checked','unverified_cross_board',false,'NOT_VERIFIED',array['AQA','Pearson Edexcel','OCR']::text[],'{}'::text[],false),
